          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT TO_TIMESTAMP(s.last_updated_ts) AS time, s.state::float AS value FROM states s JOIN states_meta sm ON s.metadata_id = sm.metadata_id WHERE sm.entity_id = 'sensor.mbptillo_battery_trend' AND s.state ~ '^-?[0-9.]+$' AND $__timeFilter(TO_TIMESTAMP(s.last_updated_ts)) ORDER BY 1",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "ha-postgres"
          },
          "legendFormat": "trend"
        }
      ],
      "description": "30-min slope from the minute cron. BAT0/status is useless as a fault signal - it flaps Charging/Discharging every 30-60 s in BOTH the healthy and failing case (max run 5 min either way). Healthy charging measures +18..+21 %/h; the 08-07/08 charger failure hit -23 %/h. Sustained < -5 %/h while AC is online fires the under-delivery alert."
    },
